      <slug></slug>
      <title>Shoes, a versatile Ruby GUI toolkit</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Ruby on Rails</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://code.whytheluckystiff.net/shoes/&#34;&gt;Shoes&lt;/a&gt; is a refreshingly new GUI toolkit for the Ruby language, written by the notorious _why.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Koen will present this shiny toolkit, including the improvements that &lt;a href=&#34;http://code.whytheluckystiff.net/shoes/&#34;&gt;Shoes&lt;/a&gt; has gone through in the recent months. If the demo-gods are benevolent, he&amp;#39;ll demo a Twitter client written in Shoes, and give a look under the hood.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2471">Koen Van der Auwera</person>
      </persons>
